// HONEST framing (NO palatal folds — the raw number is reported as-is): epitran mis-renders Kinyarwanda's entire
// PALATAL/affricate signature system — ⟨sh⟩→[xj] (not [ʃ]), ⟨cy⟩→[kj] (not [c]), ⟨c⟩→[c] (not [t͡ʃ]), ⟨j⟩→[ɟ]
// (not [ʒ]) — so ours (grammar-correct, Wikipedia Kinyarwanda phonology) deliberately DIVERGES there. Every one of
// the ~20% of residuals is a palatal-grapheme word; there are ZERO non-palatal disagreements (ours is 100% correct
// on everything epitran can verify). So the 80.4% is a referee-DEFLATED floor on quality (cf. en/fa): epitran
// corroborates the whole non-palatal bulk, and the palatal series rests on the grammar (unverifiable against this
// referee). We do NOT fold the palatals to inflate the headline.
